  "_comment": "Shared conformance corpus for the dd-policy-engine evaluators. Each vector is a dd-wls rule tree (the JSON projection of the FlatBuffers schema), a set of facts, and the expected tri-state result (TRUE/FALSE/ABSTAIN). A vector may also carry an 'actions' array and an 'expect_outcome' (inject/inject_set/tracer_versions/tracer_configs); the Go harness then decodes the policy actions and asserts the resulting Outcome. This file is the cross-engine contract: the Go harness runs it through the public API (also checking expect_outcome when present), while the C harness runs the same rule trees and compares only the tri-state result -- C actions are host callbacks with no comparable engine-level value.",
